SUMMARY:Honey Brook Fire Company Consignment Auction
DESCRIPTION:This weekend is the annual Honey Brook Auction and Mud Sale in Eastern Lancaster County. \nUp for auction this year are numerous quilts and crafts\, lots of groceries\, outdoor furniture and accessories. New household furniture\, many antiques and collectibles. New and rebuilt farm machinery\, dairy equipment\, many horses\, and heifers. Many sheds\, carriages\, buggies\, and…FOOD! \n  \nThe Honey Brook Fire Company & Consignment Auction falls on the 2nd Saturday of May every year. \n\nMud Sales are a unique Lancaster County tradition to raise funds for local volunteer fire companies. See our complete schedule of Lancaster County mud sales. \nPlease Note: Many of the Fire Companies holding mud sales can always use extra help on the days they receive items and the day of the event.  It takes a LOT of labor to put on a mud sale.
